  "title": "PsiConnect",
  "description": "PsiConnect is a multimodal neuroimaging dataset examining context-dependent neural and subjective effects of psilocybin in 62 participants scanned before and after a 19 mg dose. It combines multi-echo functional, structural and diffusion-weighted MRI with EEG during resting state and three naturalistic conditions (guided meditation, music listening, movie watching). Half of the cohort completed an 8-week meditation training program. Behavioural and self-report measures with follow-ups up to one year support study of acute and longitudinal effects.",
  "methods_description": "Participants underwent multi-echo fMRI, structural MRI, diffusion-weighted MRI and EEG before and after administration of 19 mg psilocybin, during rest, guided meditation, music listening and movie watching. Half of the participants completed an 8-week meditation training program. Behavioural and self-report batteries were collected acutely and at follow-ups up to one year.",
